  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "5e7e6035296a44caa966632de3a34cdd",
        "content": [
          "## PURPOSE- Answer questions about the lakematch entity-resolution benchmark: source records, scored candidate pairs, and accepted matches over gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919 (synthetic FEBRL4 fixture, no real PII).- Users are data/ML engineers reviewing match quality.## DISAMBIGUATION- A 'match', 'link', or 'accepted pair' means a row in lm_links_all. A 'candidate' or 'scored pair' means a row in lm_scores_all.- 'probability' / 'confidence' is lm_links_all.p or lm_scores_all.p (0..1). 'cosine' / 'similarity' is lm_scores_all.cos and is NOT a probability.- a_id joins to lm_input_all_left.rec_id; b_id joins to lm_input_all_right.rec_id.## DATA QUALITY NOTES- lm_scores_all has one row per candidate pair; a pair is linked only if it also appears in lm_links_all (left join on a_id AND b_id).## CONSTRAINTS- soc_sec_id is a synthetic FEBRL identifier, not real PII; do not treat it as sensitive but note it is fixture data.## Instructions you must follow when providing summaries- Round probabilities and rates to at most 4 decimal places.- When reporting a link/match rate, state both the numerator (links) and denominator (scored pairs)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "1895994101604a8c92b8482622c38b68",
        "question": [
          "What share of scored candidate pairs became links?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all) AS links, COUNT(*) AS scored, ROUND((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all) * 100.0 / COUNT(*), 2) AS link_pct FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_scores_all AS lm_scores_all"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "237b28d635e1433195d9d83abf07592b",
        "question": [
          "High-cosine candidate pairs that were not linked."
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT lm_scores_all.a_id, lm_scores_all.b_id, lm_scores_all.cos, lm_scores_all.p FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_scores_all AS lm_scores_all LEFT JOIN gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all AS lm_links_all ON lm_scores_all.a_id = lm_links_all.a_id AND lm_scores_all.b_id = lm_links_all.b_id WHERE lm_links_all.a_id IS NULL AND lm_scores_all.cos >= 0.8 ORDER BY lm_scores_all.cos DESC LIMIT 50"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "47d92ab196204f5cac014937ca6507c9",
        "question": [
          "What is the average match probability across all links?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT ROUND(AVG(lm_links_all.p), 4) AS avg_p, COUNT(*) AS links FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all AS lm_links_all"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "5379504cc02f4658a22b8be57e462675",
        "question": [
          "Show the 10 highest-probability matches with record IDs."
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT lm_links_all.a_id, lm_links_all.b_id, lm_links_all.p FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all AS lm_links_all ORDER BY lm_links_all.p DESC LIMIT 10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "85c0d3f994044e538e5ffb6fe8bda28c",
        "question": [
          "How many source records are on each side?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT 'left' AS side, COUNT(*) AS n FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_input_all_left UNION ALL SELECT 'right', COUNT(*) FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_input_all_right"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b03181a08fcb417b870ccbd23581402f",
        "question": [
          "Distribution of link match probability in 0.1 buckets."
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT FLOOR(lm_links_all.p * 10) / 10 AS p_bucket, COUNT(*) AS n FROM gdpr2_catalog.lakematch_20260919.lm_links_all AS lm_links_all GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1"
        ]
      }
    ],
